## Entity panel: virtual attributes move back to the Attrs. tab
================================================================================

Context:
Virtual attributes read like attributes to users (they are shown with the
entity's other values in the Knowledge Graph), so having them under
Behaviour next to functions and jobs was confusing. They now sit under the
mapped attributes in Attrs., keeping their "Computed when viewed" chip.

Changes:

1. src/front/static/ontology/js/ontology-shared-panels.js
   Virtual attributes section (``#sharedEntityVirtualAttributes``) moved
   from the Behaviour pane to the Attrs. pane, below the mapped attributes.
   Behaviour now holds Functions, Jobs and Inference rules (SWRL) only.
2. tests/units/front/test_entity_panel_tabs.py
   Attrs. holds mapped then virtual attributes with one effect chip;
   Behaviour lists its three sections and no virtual attributes.
3. docs/user-guide.md
   Virtual attribute step points at Attrs.; the Entity Panel Tabs table
   lists Attrs. = mapped then virtual attributes.

