## Entity panel: one shared section layout inside every tab
================================================================================

Context:
Sections inside the entity panel tabs each had their own markup: grey
framed boxes on some, white bordered boxes on others, help text under the
box, "Assign" / "Select" / icon-only add buttons, plain grey "No ..."
empty texts, always-bordered two-row description textareas, and native
multi-selects (Ctrl/Cmd-click) for Equivalent To / Disjoint With. All five
tabs now render their sections with one set of helpers.

Changes:

1. src/front/static/ontology/js/ontology-shared-panels.js
   - New helper block (``// ---- Panel section helpers ----``):
     ``EFFECT_CHIPS`` (single source for the four effect chips),
     ``panelSectionHeader`` (icon + title, item count, effect chip, "+ Add"
     button or a dropdown menu, one-line subtitle, info button carrying the
     long help in title/aria-label, optional ``<label for>`` title),
     ``panelEmptyState`` (dashed box with a direct "Add ..." link),
     ``panelItemRow`` (icon, title + kind badge, muted full name, remove
     button, body underneath; escapes its own text) and
     ``panelInlineField`` (borderless always-editable textarea, plain text
     when view-only). ``_updatePanelSection`` refreshes the header count and
     flips Add/Change on single-item sections (Dashboard, Dataset).
   - Pane markup: every section is ``<section class="panel-section">`` with
     the shared header; grey ``bg-light rounded border`` boxes removed;
     General puts the icon picker and the name on one row (the duplicate
     emoji preview is gone) and moves Group last; Attrs. Add is a menu
     (From data assets / Manually); all ids the rest of the code reads are
     unchanged.
   - Equivalent to / Disjoint with: chip pickers (``renderSharedAxiomChips``,
     ``addSharedAxiomChip``, ``removeSharedAxiomChip``) drive the original
     multi-selects, now hidden, so save and constraints code are unchanged;
     focus returns to the add list after each add/remove.
   - Render functions for mapped attributes, inherited relationships,
     virtual attributes, functions, jobs, inference rules, bridges,
     dashboard and dataset use the shared rows and empty states
     ("No functions yet." + "Add a function", ...). Attribute names and
     inherited relationship labels are now HTML-escaped (they were
     interpolated raw), and the inherited-relationship onclick is
     attribute-escaped.
   - Dirty tracking ignores buttons marked ``data-panel-passive`` (info
     buttons, the Add dropdown toggle, inherited-relationship links), so
     reading help no longer flags unsaved changes.
2. src/front/static/ontology/css/ontology-shared-panels.css
   Section, header, count, subtitle, help, empty state, item row, kind
   badge, inline field (transparent border at rest, border on hover, shared
   focus ring on focus), attribute row, chip picker and identity row rules,
   all on shared tokens; header actions never wrap. Removed the unused
   ``.panel-box``, ``#sharedEntityAttributes`` sizing and ``.va-group``
   rules.
3. tests/units/front/test_entity_panel_sections.py (new)
   Runs the helpers under node (header, warning chip, view-only, menu,
   label-for, empty state, item escaping, inline field) and pins the pane
   markup, chip pickers, empty states, borderless descriptions, passive
   buttons and CSS contracts (red before the change: 33 failed).
4. tests/units/front/test_entity_panel_tabs.py,
   tests/units/front/test_class_actions_ui.py,
   tests/units/front/test_inherited_relations_ui.py,
   tests/units/front/test_ontology_dataset_description.py
   Assert the helper arguments (``title:`` / ``chip:`` / ``id:``) instead of
   the old literal markup; effect chip labels defined once.
5. docs/user-guide.md
   Entity Panel Tabs section describes the section layout, in-place
   descriptions and the chip pickers; Dashboard steps use Links → + Add /
   Change.

Browser check (local dev server, testzerocopy domain, Playwright, 1440px
and 390px): all five tabs screenshotted, no horizontal overflow, header
counts filled (Attrs. 1 / 2, Functions 1, Inference rules 1), info-button
click leaves the panel clean, Equivalent-to chip add/remove updates the
hidden select and keeps focus on the add list, Attrs. menu lists both
choices, no console or page errors.

